/T (Another important feature of this system is the separation of roles between users and administrators. Users can create an account, log in, view upcoming events, book tickets, and see their booked tickets. They can also view the QR codes associated with their tickets. On the other hand, administrators have special privileges such as adding new events, updating event details, viewing ticket bookings, and validating tickets. This role-based access ensures proper control and security within the system.)
/E (Another important feature of this system is the separation of roles between users and administrators. Users can create an account, log in, view upcoming events, book tickets, and see their booked tickets. They can also view the QR codes associated with their tickets. On the other hand, administrators have special privileges such as adding new events, updating event details, viewing ticket bookings, and validating tickets. This role-based access ensures proper control and security within the system.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 292 0 R
/T (The system is designed using modern web technologies to provide a smooth and responsive user experience. The frontend is developed using React, which helps in creating interactive and user friendly web pages. The backend is developed using Spring Boot, which provides a powerful and secure framework for handling business logic, database operations, and API communication. The MySQL database is used to store information related to users, events, tickets, and QR codes. The combination of these technologies ensures that the system is reliable, scalable, and easy to maintain.)
/E (The system is designed using modern web technologies to provide a smooth and responsive user experience. The frontend is developed using React, which helps in creating interactive and user friendly web pages. The backend is developed using Spring Boot, which provides a powerful and secure framework for handling business logic, database operations, and API communication. The MySQL database is used to store information related to users, events, tickets, and QR codes. The combination of these technologies ensures that the system is reliable, scalable, and easy to maintain.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 292 0 R
/T (One of the main objectives of this project is to reduce the complexity involved in event ticket booking. With this system, users do not need to carry physical tickets, as all ticket information is stored digitally and can be accessed anytime. The QR code system allows quick and error-free ticket verification, which reduces waiting time at event entrances and improves the overall event experience. It also helps event organizers to manage large crowds efficiently.)
/E (One of the main objectives of this project is to reduce the complexity involved in event ticket booking. With this system, users do not need to carry physical tickets, as all ticket information is stored digitally and can be accessed anytime. The QR code system allows quick and error-free ticket verification, which reduces waiting time at event entrances and improves the overall event experience. It also helps event organizers to manage large crowds efficiently.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
