498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Manual ticketing systems also had many management problems. Event organizers had to maintain paper records of ticket sales, which was difficult and prone to errors. It was hard to keep track of how many tickets were sold and how many were remaining. Sometimes tickets were printed more than required, leading to confusion and loss. There was also a high chance of tickets being lost, damaged, or stolen.)
/E (Manual ticketing systems also had many management problems. Event organizers had to maintain paper records of ticket sales, which was difficult and prone to errors. It was hard to keep track of how many tickets were sold and how many were remaining. Sometimes tickets were printed more than required, leading to confusion and loss. There was also a high chance of tickets being lost, damaged, or stolen.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 293 0 R
/T (Another major problem with manual ticketing was ticket verification. At the event entrance, staff members had to manually check each ticket. This made the entry process slow and inefficient. It was also difficult to identify fake or duplicate tickets, which could lead to unauthorized entry. These issues highlighted the need for a more reliable and efficient ticket booking system.)
/E (Another major problem with manual ticketing was ticket verification. At the event entrance, staff members had to manually check each ticket. This made the entry process slow and inefficient. It was also difficult to identify fake or duplicate tickets, which could lead to unauthorized entry. These issues highlighted the need for a more reliable and efficient ticket booking system.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
