<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 294 0 R
/T (Online ticketing systems also helped event organizers manage ticket sales more effectively. They could store ticket information in databases and generate reports easily. However, many early online systems still had limitations. Although tickets were booked online, users often had to print their tickets or show screenshots at the event. This did not completely eliminate the possibility of ticket duplication or misuse.)
/E (Online ticketing systems also helped event organizers manage ticket sales more effectively. They could store ticket information in databases and generate reports easily. However, many early online systems still had limitations. Although tickets were booked online, users often had to print their tickets or show screenshots at the event. This did not completely eliminate the possibility of ticket duplication or misuse.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 294 0 R
/T (Another limitation was the lack of real-time ticket validation. Some systems did not update ticket status when a ticket was used. As a result, the same ticket could be used multiple times, leading to fraud. Additionally, some systems had poor user interfaces, making it difficult for users to navigate and complete the booking process.)
/E (Another limitation was the lack of real-time ticket validation. Some systems did not update ticket status when a ticket was used. As a result, the same ticket could be used multiple times, leading to fraud. Additionally, some systems had poor user interfaces, making it difficult for users to navigate and complete the booking process.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
