542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (In the existing system, event ticket booking is mostly done either manually or through basic online platforms. In manual systems, customers have to visit ticket counters or agents to purchase tickets. This process is time-consuming and inconvenient, especially for popular events. It also leads to long queues and crowding at ticket counters.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (Manual systems require physical tickets, which can be lost, damaged, or duplicated. There is no proper way to verify whether a ticket is genuine or already used. Event organizers must manually check each ticket at the entrance, which increases the chances of errors and unauthorized entry.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
544 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (Some online ticket booking systems are available, but many of them do not provide proper real-time ticket validation. Although users can book tickets online, they still have to show printed tickets or screenshots, which can be misused. There is also a lack of centralized control and proper tracking of ticket usage. Due to these problems, the existing system is inefficient, insecure, and difficult to manage.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
545 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 297 0 R
/T (4.2 Proposed System)
/E (4.2 Proposed System)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (The proposed Event Ticket Booking System is a web-based solution designed to overcome the limitations of the existing system. It provides a fully digital platform for booking, managing, and validating event tickets. In this system, users can register and log in to their accounts, browse available events, and book tickets online. After booking, each user receives a digital ticket with a unique QR code. This QR code is used for ticket verification at the event entrance.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
