/T (The UML diagrams used in this project include Use Case Diagram, Class Diagram, Sequence Diagram, Collaboration Diagram, and Data Flow Diagram. Each diagram represents a different view of the system and helps in better understanding of the overall architecture. The Use Case Diagram describes the interaction between actors and the system. In this project there are two main actors: User and Admin. The user can register, login, view events, book tickets, view booked tickets, and access the QR code. The admin can login, add or update events, view bookings, and validate tickets using QR code scanning. This diagram defines the major functionalities provided by the system.)
/E (The UML diagrams used in this project include Use Case Diagram, Class Diagram, Sequence Diagram, Collaboration Diagram, and Data Flow Diagram. Each diagram represents a different view of the system and helps in better understanding of the overall architecture. The Use Case Diagram describes the interaction between actors and the system. In this project there are two main actors: User and Admin. The user can register, login, view events, book tickets, view booked tickets, and access the QR code. The admin can login, add or update events, view bookings, and validate tickets using QR code scanning. This diagram defines the major functionalities provided by the system.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
