/T (The project was designed, developed, and tested to provide an efficient digital platform for managing events and ticketing operations. The system replaces the traditional manual ticket booking process with an automated solution, allowing users to browse events, book tickets online, and receive a unique QR code that acts as a digital entry pass. The integration of QR code technology ensures secure and reliable verification at the event venue.)
/E (The project was designed, developed, and tested to provide an efficient digital platform for managing events and ticketing operations. The system replaces the traditional manual ticket booking process with an automated solution, allowing users to browse events, book tickets online, and receive a unique QR code that acts as a digital entry pass. The integration of QR code technology ensures secure and reliable verification at the event venue.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 343 0 R
/T (The main objective of this project was to develop a system that reduces manual work, prevents ticket duplication, and provides real-time validation. These objectives have been achieved through the implementation of modern technologies such as React for frontend, Spring Boot for backend, and MySQL for database management. The system allows users to register, log in, view events, select seats, make payments, and access their ticket details from anywhere. The admin module provides complete control over event creation, ticket management, and QR validation.)
/E (The main objective of this project was to develop a system that reduces manual work, prevents ticket duplication, and provides real-time validation. These objectives have been achieved through the implementation of modern technologies such as React for frontend, Spring Boot for backend, and MySQL for database management. The system allows users to register, log in, view events, select seats, make payments, and access their ticket details from anywhere. The admin module provides complete control over event creation, ticket management, and QR validation.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 343 0 R
/T (One of the major advantages of this system is the QR code validation mechanism. Each ticket contains a unique QR code generated at the time of booking. At the event entrance, the QR code is scanned and verified with the database. If the ticket is valid, entry is granted; otherwise, the system rejects duplicate or fake tickets. This feature increases security and eliminates unauthorized access to events. It also reduces the need for physical tickets and manual checking.)
/E (One of the major advantages of this system is the QR code validation mechanism. Each ticket contains a unique QR code generated at the time of booking. At the event entrance, the QR code is scanned and verified with the database. If the ticket is valid, entry is granted; otherwise, the system rejects duplicate or fake tickets. This feature increases security and eliminates unauthorized access to events. It also reduces the need for physical tickets and manual checking.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
